<title>USA: GOLF-SECOND ROUND SCORES AT SPRINT INTERNATIONAL.</title>
<headline>GOLF-SECOND ROUND SCORES AT SPRINT INTERNATIONAL.</headline>
<dateline>CASTLE ROCK, Colorado 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading scores</p>
<p>when play was halted during the second round of the $1.7</p>
<p>million Sprint International golf tournament on Friday.</p>
<p>Scoring according to Modified Stableford format, which</p>
<p>awards five points for eagle, two for birdie, zero for par,</p>
<p>and subtracts one point for bogey and three points for double</p>
<p>bogey or worse (Players U.S. unless noted):</p>
<p>27 points - Phil Mickelson 14 13</p>
<p>23 - Larry Mize 8 15</p>
<p>22 - Neal Lancaster 8 14, Skip Kendall 10 12</p>
<p>20 - Nick Price (Zimbabwe) 6 14</p>
<p>19 - Jay Haas 15 4, Stuart Appleby (Australia) 9 10</p>
<p>18 - Tom Lehman 13 5, Kirk Triplett 8 10, Greg Norman</p>
<p>(Australia) 9 9, Brad Faxon 10 8</p>
<p>17 - Kevin Sutherland 3 14, Pete Jordan 6 11</p>
<p>16 - Andrew Magee 11 5, Tom Purtzer -4 20, Tommy Armour 8 8,</p>
<p>Olin Brown 10 6</p>
<p>15 - Kenny Perry 9 6, Dave Stockton junior 12 3</p>
<p>14 - Emlyn Aubrey 4 10</p>
<p>13 - Mark Calcavecchia 4 9, Gary Hallberg 8 5, John Huston 6</p>
<p>7, Davis Love 5 8, Dan Forsman 3 10</p>
<p>Add non-U.S. scores:</p>
<p>4 - Retief Goosen (South Africa) 5 -1</p>
<p>3 - Peter Lonard 5 -2</p>
<p>2 - Yutaka Hagawa (Japan) 3 -1</p>
<p>-1 - Rafael Alarcon (Mexico) -3 2</p>
<p>-9 - Phil Tataurangi (New Zealand) -12 3</p>
</text>
